4.1. HR records management:
— recording employee data;
— preparation of analyses and reports;
— preparation of personnel orders;
— maintaining personal employee cards;
— filling in, accounting for and storing employment records;
— calculating work experience;
— drawing up vacation schedules;
— transferring documents to the archive.

4.2. Selection and placement of personnel:
— planning of vacancies;
— selection of candidates;
— organisation of employment;
— communication with employment centres.

4.3. Conducting activities to improve employee qualifications.
4.4. Ensuring compliance with labour legislation and preparing relevant documents.
4.5. Developing proposals for employee incentives and motivation.
4.6. Preparing proposals for changes to the staffing schedule.
4.7. Advising employees on labour relations matters.
